error[ffi_constant_type]: `SHIFT_PAST` in `fixedbugs-2072-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 2: shift count >= width of type
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2072-a-value-c-leaves-undefined-is-told.hero:14:5
     |
  14 |     constant SHIFT_PAST: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2072-values.h` line 2 reads `#define SHIFT_PAST (1 << 40)`
  note: C leaves this value undefined: a program reading `SHIFT_PAST` would read whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines

